content:
Sam K: quick question on chat/completions contract — how should the API treat messages[] items that omit `role`? breaking change if we start rejecting, but ambiguous if we default. thoughts?

Jess L.: my vote: reject (400) for new major version but offer a compatibility window. for patch/minor we should accept and default -> `user`. defaulting silently feels risky though. :thinking:

Mike O'Neil: leaning toward accept+default to `user` for now. lots of clients produce {content:..., name:...} historically. if we add a header/param like `x-allow-role-default=true` we can ramp.

Rachel T.: also think about streaming behavior — streaming deltas should not keep re-sending role on each chunk. propose: first chunk may include `role` (only if present in source message), subsequent `delta` chunks only contain `content`/`tool_call` fragments. that keeps client impls simpler.

Sam K: good point. for tool/function-calling: should `function_call` object require `name` when `type: tool_call`? current spec allows name optional (to indicate any tool), but some backends need explicit name to route. suggest `name` optional but add `routing_hint` field. example: 
```json
{"message": {"role":"user","content":"run search"},
 "function_call": {"type":"tool_call","name":null, "args":{}}}
```

Jess L.: example schema suggestion (for API docs):
```json
{"type":"object","properties":{
  "messages":{"type":"array","items":{
    "type":"object","properties":{
      "role":{"type":"string","enum":["system","user","assistant"],"nullable":false},
      "name":{"type":"string"},
      "content":{"type":"string"},
      "function_call":{"type":"object","properties":{
         "type":{"type":"string"},
         "name":{"type":["string","null"]},
         "args":{"type":"object"}
      }}
    }
  }}
}}
```
Note: `role` non-nullable in new spec; for backward compat accept missing but emit warning header.

Mike O'Neil: rollout plan idea: 1) server accepts missing `role` and defaults -> `user`, 2) emit `Warning: missing-role-defaulted` response header, 3) after 2 months, switch to 400 for requests that omit `role` unless client sets `X-Allow-Deprecated-MessageShape: true`. works?

Rachel T.: QA checklist: create short evals for: message parsing, streaming reassembly, function_call partials, SDKs (python/js/go) behavior. I'll add items to the chat-contract epic. pinging @eng-runtime for kernel/streaming impacts.

eng-runtime-bot: FYI — streaming delta change might affect continuous-batching. runtime team please confirm whether emitting `role` only once per response is already safe for KV-cache pointers.

deploy-bot: canary rollout scheduled: 2034567920 — will include `warning` header and defaulting behavior. roll forward if no errors in 4h.

Sam K.: thanks all — I'll open the PR with the schema snippet + rollout notes and tag reviewers (jess, mike, rachel). please thumbs up on PR when ready. :thumbsup:
